# Keep Git's line-ending conversion away from binary files.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on the Windows dev machine, so without these rules Git
# treats every file as text and rewrites CRLF/LF byte pairs on add and checkout.
# In a PDF or an image those bytes are content, not line endings, and rewriting
# them corrupts the file. Marking a type `binary` also stops Git diffing it as
# text (commits read "Bin 3421 -> 3563 bytes" instead of bogus line counts).
#
# Tracked today: 24 PDFs in public/downloads, 1 PNG, 1 ICO.
# The jpg/woff2 lines are pre-emptive — the failure mode is silent, so the rule
# should already exist the first time one is added.

# Default: treat files as text and normalise line endings in the repo.
# This MUST come first — later rules win, so the binary rules below override it.
* text=auto

# Binary types: never convert bytes, never diff as text.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff2 binary
